text: "# Triage, Priorities & Goals\n\nHow to spend limited engagement time well — what to do first, who to focus on, and how to know it's\nworking (without WoopSocial analytics).\n\n## Triage: the priority order\n\nWhen time is short, do the highest-return things first:\n\n1. **Golden-hour comments on your fresh post** — first ~15–20 min; biggest reach lever.\n2. **DMs** — relationships and conversions live here; reply while warm.\n3. **Negative / urgent** — complaints, mistakes, anything time-sensitive; acknowledge fast, take\n   specifics private (→ `reply-and-comment-writer`); route a real crisis to `crisis-and-moderation`.\n4. **Older comments** still worth a thoughtful reply.\n5. **Proactive comments** — add value on ICP/peer/leader posts (borrows audience).\n6. **Skip:** spam and trolls — delete/ignore; don't feed them.\n\n### Worked example — \"I have 15 minutes\"\n\nReply to every comment on the post that went out an hour ago (golden-hour leftovers) → answer the 2 new\nDMs → one quick, genuine reply to a complaint with \"let's sort this in DMs\" → if time remains, one\nvalue-adding comment on a niche leader's post. Stop. Done beats perfect.\n\n## The right people, not vanity\n\nEngagement should reach **the people who matter to the business** — your ICP and niche peers — not\nmaximize raw volume. A flood of comments from the wrong crowd (or from bait) doesn't build anything.\n**Make every interaction count**; engage where it compounds.\n\n## Map to a goal (and signals you can actually see)\n\nPick a **goal** for engagement — relationships, leads, community, support — and **2–3 meaningful\nsignals**, not vanity metrics:\n\n- **Comment depth** (real conversations, not just \"🔥\").\n- **DM conversations started** (and where they lead).\n- **Replies to your replies** / people coming back.\n- **Proactive comments that sparked a reply** (the audience-borrowing working).\n\n**Honesty about measurement:** inbox depth is read **natively** (WoopSocial has no inbox). Post\nmetrics for the covered platforms come from WoopSocial via `analytics-and-reporting`. **Never fabricate performance\ndata or promise a specific number.** Engagement is a leading indicator; judge it by depth and direction\nover weeks, not by a vanity count today.\n\n## What to stop doing\n\n- Chasing likes/followers as the scoreboard (they're the weakest signal).\n- Replying to everything everywhere (spreading thin) instead of the right things well.\n- Engagement bait (\"comment YES\") and pods — detected and penalized (→ `linkedin-growth`).\n- Buying/automating engagement — fake, detected, self-defeating (see the SKILL's no-automation rule).\n"
